Q: 2 column grid, multiple rows in one. How do I make them equal in height? A: <p>This should get you started:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div id="image_box" class="row"&gt;
    &lt;div class="small-6 large-6 columns left-col"&gt;
        &lt;div class="row"&gt;
            &lt;div class="large-12 columns"&gt;
                &lt;img src="http://placehold.it/200x100"  /&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="row"&gt;
            &lt;div class="large-12 columns"&gt;
                &lt;img src="http://placehold.it/200x100" /&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="row"&gt;
            &lt;div class="large-12 columns"&gt;
                &lt;img src="http://placehold.it/200x100" /&gt;
            &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;

    &lt;div class="small-6 large-6 columns"&gt;
        &lt;img src="http://placehold.it/200x340" /&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;style type="text/css"&gt;
.left-col img { margin-bottom:20px; float:right;}
&lt;/style&gt;
</code></pre>

